  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Adding support for all kinds of controllers is troublesome with the growth of VR accessories and without a clear standard... However why not give some power to the people who want to express themselves in more ways (just like how vive trackers are now a thing) and have a controller option called \"Joystick fingers\" or something alike where people can figure their own ways out to map to those fingers (Virtual joysticks etc) without the need for a lower level scripting access which has risks of it's own. Joystick is great because they are analog inputs by default and easily accessible to many users (No weird streaming required per se)",
